{
  "about": [
    "FL-883 known-bad file corpus: server/test/medium/specs/corpus/known-bad-corpus.spec.ts runs every file through metadata extraction, thumbnail generation and (videos) the playback encode, and compares what happened with `expect`.",
    "root: `test-assets` is e2e/test-assets (scripts/checkout-test-assets.sh), `fixtures` is server/test/fixtures.",
    "outcome per step: ok | skipped | library-care (thumbnail handed to Library care) | set-aside (failed until FL-845 set it aside; `cause` is the stored cause) | failed.",
    "Only the keys written under a step are compared. metadata: dateTimeOriginal, localDateTime, timeZone, width, height, orientation, videoCodec. thumbnail: preview, thumbnail (WxH). encode: videoCodec, size (WxH).",
    "To add a file: the fixture repositories are public, so use only a file with a clear licence (CC0, public domain, a permissive licence, or one generated here). Add an entry with file, root, type, note, source, licence, reproduces and an outcome for each step; run `mise run //server:corpus`; check the entry in the report it writes (known-bad-corpus-actual.json) and copy the facts you want pinned into `expect`."
  ],
